 "text": "Hi, how are you? Keep it simple. Start and end it with background music of your partner's choice, so it feels like your shared space. Welcome guests in the living room, rather than in the room itself.mate or close friend would be the natural choice, since they know both partners well. Ask them to start with how they met, where you lived, and any key dates. Certainly. Ask each other for a rematch, if you' been together for years. Then, after the ceremony, everyone goes into the living room together, instead of each one you with their partner. Then, see the garden together for the first time, holding onto each other but looking at each other. That's the rematch. Keep it brief, five minutes tops. A traditional ceremony or a poem would feel like overdoing it in your situation.",
